INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION CORRECTION
- Confirmed defect: `system.launch` supplied `~tag_topic`, but the runtime node hardcoded `/tag_detections`; map, AMCL, and global costmap subscriptions were also literals.
- Red node-level command: `source devel/setup.bash && ROS_MASTER_URI=http://127.0.0.1:11311 ROS_IP=127.0.0.1 rostest multifloor_manager node_wiring.test --results-filename task11-wiring-red.xml`.
- Red result: 1 failure. Live graph subscribers were `/tag_detections`, `/map`, `/amcl_pose`, and `/move_base/global_costmap/costmap`; none of the supplied `/fixture/*` topics were registered.
- Fix: runtime subscriptions now honor `~tag_topic`, `~map_topic`, `~amcl_pose_topic`, and `~global_costmap_topic`, preserving source-compatible defaults and queue sizes. Existing private parameters remain in force for action name, initial-pose publisher, service timeout, change-map, nomotion, and clear-costmaps services. Fixed `/multifloor/floor_state` remains the declared public state endpoint.
- Green node-level rostest launched the real sole node with non-default topics and passed 1/1. No extra node or readiness gate was added.
- Added root-false regression: required false observations continue through the sole explicit root until the evaluator's timeout, producing ABORTED/FAULT with trace reason `timeout`.
- Preserved adapter cases: true explicit root and eight feedback phases; ignored false callback observations cannot veto; cancellation preempts and fences late writes; service failure aborts and fences late writes.
- Full sourced root unittest suite: 49/49 pass. Condition engine: 23/23 pass. Multifloor package: 14/14 pass. Interface/package focused suite: 13/13 pass. `catkin_make`: pass. `catkin_make run_tests`: pass.
